Task 1 — Fix #770: `/extract` corrupts source files (product, src/commands_refactor.rs)
find_symbol_block counts braces with a bare for ch in line.chars() and no literal/comment state, and extract_symbol uses that range to delete lines from the source. A println!("}") truncates the block → source left with unbalanced braces and the target gets a fragment; a println!("{") swallows the next function. Both silent — the preview shows the same wrong block the write uses. One pure significant_braces(line, &mut in_block_comment) -> Vec<char> helper (braces in order, so } fn other() { still works), covering string/char literals with escapes, Rust lifetimes (the #759 trap — don't repeat it), //, /* */ across lines, and raw strings. Tests at the emission point: after extract_symbol, assert both files.

